    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "To further the investigation of syntactic variation in spoken language from a comparative perspective,\r\ntwo comprehensive and homogeneously annotated datasets are provided for the genitive and dative alternations in four spoken varieties of English: American English (AmE), British English (BrE), Canadian English (CanE), and New Zealand English (NZE).  Documentation provides the sources, inclusion criteria, and annotation schemata for the datasets, as well as key references.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "BRESNAN, JOAN, ROSENBACH, ANETTE, SZMRECSANYI, BENEDIKT, TAGLIAMONTE, SALI A. and TODD, SIMON.  (2017). Syntactic alternations data: datives and genitives in four varieties of English. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/qj187zs3852",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Preferred Citation",
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Szmrecsanyi, B., Grafmiller, J., Bresnan, J., Rosenbach, A., Tagliamonte, S., and Todd, S. (2017). Spoken syntax in a comparative perspective: The dative and genitive alternation in varieties of English. Glossa: a journal of general linguistics, 2(1), 86. DOI: http://doi.org/10.5334/gjgl.310",
            "type": "citation/reference",
            "identifier": [],
